# bash scripts must stay LF: they run in CI (Linux) and in Git Bash / WSL on Windows, where CRLF
# line endings break them ("set: pipefail: invalid option name", "\r': No such file or directory").
# With core.autocrlf=true (the Windows default this repo is often cloned with) every checkout
# converts them to CRLF; this file forces them back to LF in the working tree as well.
*.sh text eol=lf
